1
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:04,317
As we all travel across the sea,

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,660
raising our voices, we take
in the beautiful blue world.

3
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:12,237
Our spirits ready to
go, everybody rejoices.

4
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:15,740
Now let's go, get the sails all unfurled.

5
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:19,980
La la la la la.

6
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:21,680
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

7
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:25,440
Here we are in between
the sea and the sky.

8
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:28,817
Ready now for adventure,
we're itching to try.

9
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:30,457
Get ready to roam.

10
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:32,177
So all aboard now!

11
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:33,897
We're set to go.

12
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:36,977
Set sail to the ocean so deep!

13
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:40,217
Ready for a truly grand adventure!

14
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:42,037
Well, don't you think?

15
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,737
That sounds really fun!

16
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:45,597
All this excitement!

17
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,117
Second to none!

18
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:49,877
As we all travel across the sea!

19
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:51,217
Raising our voices!

20
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:54,217
We take in the beautiful blue world!

21
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,097
Our spirits ready to go!

22
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:57,837
Everybody rejoices!

23
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:01,380
Now let's go get the sales all unfurled!

24
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:11,637
If there's something that
I just won't ever forget!

25
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:15,197
It's the way that I felt
when our journey was set!

26
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,777
Now I won't be scared!

27
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:20,157
As long as I keep that feeling there!

28
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:23,377
With that, let us keep up the pace!

29
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:26,957
While enjoying every
trip from place to place!

30
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:30,037
Our timid hearts get the rhythm and great!

31
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:33,497
So let's keep going, adventure awaits!

32
00:01:33,580 --> 00:01:35,797
So many treasures await!

33
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:38,317
So now let's raise our voices in pride!

34
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,637
Laughing out when they are found!

35
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:44,217
With all the riches in
hand, everybody rejoices!

36
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:46,840
Party on, cause we stand tall and proud!

37
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:50,957
Life is adventurous, be
aware it's dangerous!

38
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:52,980
Who's gonna be one of us?

39
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,437
And a trip goes on because.

40
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:56,177
We're the pirates of the mouse.

41
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:57,877
To the west, to the east.

42
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:00,697
Gotta find my way, sail away,
all the way to one piece.

43
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:03,177
Bring all your dreams with
you now, fill the void.

44
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:04,837
In your heart, spread your wings.

45
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:07,057
And believe that you can soar.

46
00:02:07,140 --> 00:02:08,957
Just let the breeze guide the way.

47
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:11,497
Till you're ready to start up once again.

48
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:13,317
Now you're ready for more.

49
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,517
So many treasures await.

50
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:18,057
So now let's raise our voices in pride.

51
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:20,357
Laughing out when they are found.

52
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:22,217
With all the riches in hand.

53
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:24,737
Everybody rejoices, party on.

54
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:26,600
Cause we stand tall and proud.

55
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,357
Hey, you're back.

56
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:35,757
I thought you were too hurt to fight.

57
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:36,717
Did something happen?

58
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:38,177
You look a lot better now.

59
00:02:38,260 --> 00:02:39,697
You really saved my life back there.

60
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:40,610
That was scary.

61
00:02:40,693 --> 00:02:41,523
It's true.

62
00:02:41,606 --> 00:02:45,397
I was seriously injured when I dragged
myself to the kitchen to acquire the salt,

63
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:47,437
but then something most
fortuitous happened.

64
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:49,620
I discovered some delicious milk,

65
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:52,878
which I promptly consumed,
thus recovering my health.

66
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:55,680
Calcium doesn't act that fast. Come on!

67
00:02:56,420 --> 00:02:58,137
So there you have it, everyone.

68
00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:00,920
Milk can heal your broken bones! Lair!

69
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:04,476
Anyway, we have the salt we need now.

70
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:08,017
This should be enough to purify that
giant, but it might be a close call.

71
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:10,997
And speaking of close calls, it
looks like the kitchen's blocked off.

72
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:13,777
In other words, we only
get one chance to do this.

73
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:15,217
We don't have much time.

74
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:16,160
Let's move it.

75
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:19,637
If we don't want to melt when the
sun rises, we have two objectives.

76
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:23,720
We're gonna feed the salt to that
monster, and we gotta beat Moria.

77
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:36,737
You wanted a chance to get
your shadows back from me.

78
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:37,780
Well, here I am.

79
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:38,920
Go ahead and try.

80
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:42,657
But I'll warn you, I'm more than
just a passenger, nor a stomach.

81
00:03:42,740 --> 00:03:45,977
When I'm done with you, you'll
wish you'd melted away in the sun.

82
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:48,880
I'll show you what real
nightmares are made of!

83
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:57,437
Thank you for this chance, Straw Hats.

84
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:00,937
I swear that I shall fight beside
you with every ounce of my might.

85
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:03,117
Although this small
gesture scarcely repays

86
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:04,977
the debt I owe you for
recovering my shadow,

87
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:06,857
I shall offer what assistance I can.

88
00:04:06,940 --> 00:04:07,770
Now let's go!

89
00:04:09,860 --> 00:04:10,690
Ouch.

90
00:04:10,773 --> 00:04:12,757
We don't need you breaking any more bones,

91
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:15,487
so just hold on to the
salt and take it easy.

92
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,597
I got a few tricks up my sleeves.

93
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:19,840
Let's try my anti-monster shells.

94
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:23,240
All right, pal.

95
00:04:23,580 --> 00:04:25,877
If my last shot was too small, try this.

96
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:26,997
Franky, are you ready?

97
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:30,492
We're gonna light this zombie
up with my special oil star.

98
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:32,470
Sweet.

99
00:04:32,553 --> 00:04:33,460
Here I go.

100
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:39,370
Ignite!

101
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:41,230
Supersize...

102
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:42,640
Firebird star!

103
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:47,660
You'll be fine.

104
00:04:48,020 --> 00:04:49,617
Don't let a little fire get to you.

105
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:52,337
Those feelings of pain are
nothing but lingering memories.

106
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:55,117
From back when you were
alive, it's all in your head.

107
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:57,937
Zombies don't have to worry
about any of that nonsense.

108
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:00,117
Just calm down and put out the fire.

109
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:01,030
You'll see.

110
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:04,580
This is our chance, Zoro. Come on! Got it.

111
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:19,560
All right, green sword style!

112
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:22,700
Great Buddha Duck!

113
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:29,440
My turn, Jango Cannon!

114
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:46,380
Take this!

115
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:53,180
It's coming straight at us!

116
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,922
Vente Floor should do the trick.

117
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,720
Damn it! No fair!

118
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:12,740
He's using our own attacks against us!

119
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:14,742
Sorry about that, you guys okay?

120
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:18,580
Hold my new weapon, the Stern Beetle!

121
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:22,590
Hell yeah!

122
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:24,388
I'm ready whenever you are!

123
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:28,057
Just a word of warning, I haven't
had a chance to test this thing,

124
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:30,477
so I don't know what will
happen when I let it loose!

125
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,497
You think I can't handle this, bro?

126
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:34,180
I'm extra super this week.

127
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:35,673
I got it under control.

128
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:37,840
All right, then get in. Roger.

129
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:41,908
Shoot me straight into that
thing's stomach, and we got this.

130
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:45,780
Special attack.

131
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:47,400
Iron Man's coming.

132
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:50,210
Nice.

133
00:06:50,293 --> 00:06:51,906
Now this is some super speed.

134
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:53,070
Get ready.

135
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:56,397
This border cannon of
mine was specially made

136
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:58,797
to take down sea kings and jerks like you.

137
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:02,900
I'm going to wipe that slug
grin right off your face, Moria!

138
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:08,340
I keep forgetting he's so fast.

139
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:12,265
He might not look like him, but
he's got Luffy's moves for sure.

140
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,220
Franky, no! Oh!

141
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:29,260
Please, don't die!

142
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:37,660
Don't stop now, Oz.

143
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:40,297
That was a nice shot, but
I'm afraid he's still alive.

144
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:41,909
Why don't you stop on him?

145
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:43,550
Okay.

146
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:51,950
Ooh!

147
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:00,217
Dammit, he's gonna finish him off!

148
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:01,130
Stop!

149
00:08:01,213 --> 00:08:02,043
He can't even move!

150
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:04,150
Thunderbolt!

151
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,380
Look, that cloud!

152
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:08,170
Tempo!

153
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:12,700
Nice shot, but where did it come from?

154
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,720
Lightning, it has to be her.

155
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,412
That's the climb attack.

156
00:08:16,540 --> 00:08:18,952
Don't know where she is, but Nami's fine.

157
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:23,580
What was that flash? Was it lightning?

158
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:24,880
Oh, frightening.

159
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:26,457
That must have been Orr's.

160
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:28,540
I mean, he can do anything, right?

161
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,260
There she is.

162
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:33,400
It's Nami.

163
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:36,464
Could you stop yelling already?

164
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,537
Now they're going to know where I am.

165
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:39,980
She yelled at me.

166
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:41,360
She yelled at me.

167
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:43,400
Just like old times.

168
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:45,060
I'm so glad you're safe.

169
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:46,720
Yell at me more, Nami.

170
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:48,881
I'm so sorry I couldn't save you.

171
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:50,137
You can tell me I'll
screw what I am all right.

172
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:51,279
Would you shut up?

173
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:54,940
It's the gun!

174
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:56,580
See, I told you!

175
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:57,960
Gun-gun!

176
00:08:58,680 --> 00:08:59,510
Huh?

177
00:08:59,593 --> 00:09:00,737
Wait, he's not going to stretch, is he?

178
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:01,650
I mean, Danny?

179
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:03,620
It shouldn't reach her, right?

180
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,030
Usopp, hurry!

181
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:06,797
You've got to get Franky out of here!

182
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:07,710
Right!

183
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:10,740
It's the gun!

184
00:09:19,740 --> 00:09:20,570
What?

185
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,900
He stretched! Impossible!

186
00:09:29,220 --> 00:09:30,340
It worked!

187
00:09:30,780 --> 00:09:33,240
That was new, but it doesn't feel new.

188
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:37,777
You've got to be kidding me!

189
00:09:37,860 --> 00:09:38,690
No!

190
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:43,997
Look, up there!

191
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:44,960
She's okay!

192
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,540
She sure is screaming a lot,
but at least Robin caught her.

193
00:09:55,940 --> 00:09:57,317
That was certainly a surprise.

194
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:58,897
You're not hurt, are you?

195
00:09:58,980 --> 00:10:01,157
No, just shaking up.

196
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,540
Thank you.

197
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:06,437
I don't get it, but I
know it can't be good.

198
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:08,777
Two people can't have the
same Devil Fruit power.

199
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:12,566
Even if he has Luffy's shadow,
he shouldn't be able to do that.

200
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:20,720
It's Moria.

201
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,697
Must have been one of his tricks.

202
00:10:22,780 --> 00:10:24,260
I'm gonna kill that guy.

203
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,540
Now come, go!

204
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:31,377
Well, this is just great.

205
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:33,617
Now he's really like a
giant monster, Luffy.

206
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:34,530
Stop it, Luffy.

207
00:10:34,613 --> 00:10:36,482
You're destroying your own crew!

208
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:38,677
I'm kinda in a hurry here, okay?

209
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:39,857
What do you want with me?

210
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:43,797
Yeah, sorry to bug you like this, but
this is really important, I promise.

211
00:10:43,880 --> 00:10:45,477
We'll only take a second of your time.

212
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:47,357
We've been looking all
over the place for you.

213
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:48,740
You're our only hope.

214
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:51,537
They call the two of
us the Risky Brothers.

215
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:53,577
The gang here is the Rolling Pirates.

216
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:55,337
And our captain is Lola, the Proposer.

217
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:58,497
You want to get back to the mansion
pronto so you can beat up Gecko Moria?

218
00:10:58,580 --> 00:10:59,480
Right, pal?

219
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:04,917
Yeah, that's right Now could you
tell me what you want with me?

220
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:05,937
Listen, you're in luck.

221
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:08,557
Because we just happen to know
the secret to taking out Moria!

222
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:10,797
We can give you the power to do it, too.

223
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:13,920
And all you gotta do
is kick his ass for us.

224
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:15,137
What are you, a secret?

225
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:16,840
Give me power? Yep.

226
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:20,300
Seriously, who the hell are you guys?

227
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:26,180
Allow us to introduce you to the captain
of the Rolling Pirates, Lola the Proposer.

228
00:11:26,620 --> 00:11:29,720
Current proposal count 4,443.

229
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,160
Oh, my, aren't you handsome.

230
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:34,340
Will you marry me? No, thanks.

231
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:37,570
Rejected!

232
00:11:37,653 --> 00:11:39,820
That's 4,444!

233
00:11:40,020 --> 00:11:41,314
Better luck next time!

234
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:42,770
Anyway,

235
00:11:42,860 --> 00:11:45,017
Moria took all the
Rolling Pirate's shadows,

236
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:48,257
so we're stuck wandering this
forest till someone gets him back.

237
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:49,877
Yeah, well, he took my shadow, too.

238
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:51,017
That's why I'm in a hurry.

239
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:53,865
I won't take no for an
answer, Straw Hat Luffy.

240
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:54,960
You're a hero.

241
00:11:55,260 --> 00:11:56,777
In all of Thriller Bart's history,

242
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:59,860
nobody has been able to
wreak as much havoc as you.

243
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:04,457
You walloped the Mysterious Three,
returned some of the stolen shadows,

244
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:06,257
and caused tons of property damage.

245
00:12:06,340 --> 00:12:08,477
We've had nothing but
misery in this crappy

246
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:11,077
place till you showed up
and started kicking ass.

247
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:14,557
On the downside, it's kind of your fault
that they brought Oars back to life.

248
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:15,837
That maybe wasn't so great.

249
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:19,297
We have a whole network of victims, so
we know everything that's going on here.

250
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:21,977
We've been stuck here without
our shadows for three years.

251
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:24,497
I don't want to spend the rest
of my life on this stupid ship.

252
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:26,997
If you guys beat Merde up for
us, we could all get out of here?

253
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:29,157
and finally see the sun
again after all this time.

254
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:31,357
But we've got another problem right now.

255
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:33,657
Merde is making things
even tougher than usual.

256
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:34,817
You know where the bastard's at?

257
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:38,000
He's camped out inside
Orr's stomach. No way!

258
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:40,660
Did Orr's eat Moria? It's complicated.

259
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:43,237
He's in there piloting him like a ship.

260
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:46,477
Anyway, the point is, you're going to have
to take out that giant with your shadow.

261
00:12:46,560 --> 00:12:49,357
Otherwise, you won't be able
to lay a finger on Moria.

262
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:51,577
But I figure you would
want to beat him anyway,

263
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:53,837
since he's giving your crew a
pounding out in the courtyard.

264
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:54,861
Are you serious?

265
00:12:55,340 --> 00:12:57,737
Damn it, I gotta help
them before it's too late!

266
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:58,660
Not so fast!

267
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:03,037
Just sit tight for one second
and we'll show you our trick.

268
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:05,220
Trust me, you are gonna love this!

269
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:07,635
All right, boys, bring out the shadow!

270
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:08,890
Roger!

271
00:13:08,973 --> 00:13:09,803
Stay out of the way!

272
00:13:09,886 --> 00:13:11,092
Shadow's coming through!

273
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:13,110
Hm?

274
00:13:13,193 --> 00:13:14,023
You can grab them?

275
00:13:14,106 --> 00:13:15,277
Once they're separated, yeah.

276
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:18,377
When you feed the zombies a little
bit of salt and they come flying out,

277
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:22,317
you can just nab them out of the air
with your bare hands, no problem.

278
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:23,780
Hee-ho! Ah!

279
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:25,120
What are you doing?!

280
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:26,670
Stay still!

281
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:31,570
Stop it!

282
00:13:31,653 --> 00:13:32,929
I feel like I'm gonna die!

283
00:13:36,220 --> 00:13:41,500
All right it's in so how is it you
didn't lose consciousness did you

284
00:13:47,260 --> 00:13:51,860
I'm fine all right i guess that's
a start can you use a sword

285
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:56,060
No not as far as i know bring the sword

286
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:11,440
Wait, how did I do that?

287
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:13,857
It's quite simple.

288
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:16,017
The shadow we just
stuffed inside you used to

289
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:18,317
belong to a powerful
swordsman from the Navy.

290
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,377
It's like Moria did with my shadow.

291
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:24,357
Yeah, but since you're still alive, it adds
the shadow's fighting power to your own.

292
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:26,197
The point is, as long
as you don't pass out,

293
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:28,477
we can stuff as many
shadows in you as we got.

294
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:30,377
Ever since we figured out Moria's powers,

295
00:14:30,460 --> 00:14:32,657
we've been waiting for the
chance to turn them against him.

296
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:35,269
With a little boost,
you'll be unstoppable.

297
00:14:36,020 --> 00:14:38,637
We still have a whole
bunch of shadows left, too.

298
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:40,697
As long as you're tough
enough to withstand them,

299
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:42,137
we can give you as many as you want?

300
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:44,514
and your power will grow with each one.

301
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:47,697
Okay, but why do you have so
many shadows in the first place?

302
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:51,257
The idea was to purify a bunch of
zombies and find our own shadows,

303
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:52,170
not collect them.

304
00:14:52,253 --> 00:14:54,157
But even if we didn't
know who they belonged to,

305
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:56,677
it didn't seem right to
leave them with the zombies.

306
00:14:56,760 --> 00:15:00,197
So we thought, what the hell, might
as well take them back with us.

307
00:15:00,280 --> 00:15:03,317
There's one important thing you've
got to remember about this, though.

308
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:06,377
As you know, putting a shadow
in a corpse makes a zombie.

309
00:15:06,460 --> 00:15:09,317
But if your body still has a soul,
the shadow won't stick around.

310
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:11,857
You'll only be powered
up for about ten minutes.

311
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:16,037
After that, all the shadows fly out
and go back to their original owners.

312
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:17,180
You got it, pal?

313
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:18,877
Just ten minutes, sink or swim.

314
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,737
We'll give you every shadow we nab,

315
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:23,217
so you should be pretty
powerful when we're done.

316
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:24,220
That's a lot!

317
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:26,857
Shadows are not the fogs clearing up.

318
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:30,577
We only have about 20 minutes before the
sun rises and roasts all of us anyway.

319
00:15:30,660 --> 00:15:32,437
Our lives are in your hands.

320
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:34,117
Steal your mind, Straw Hat.

321
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,897
When we tried this trick before,

322
00:15:35,980 --> 00:15:37,977
we could only handle two
or three shadows ourselves.

323
00:15:38,060 --> 00:15:41,180
But you should be able to
do 20 or 30, no problem.

324
00:15:42,740 --> 00:15:44,140
Go for it, boys!

325
00:15:46,060 --> 00:15:47,640
I didn't agree to this!

326
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:49,291
They're really slow down!

327
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:57,940
I had no idea this was possible.

328
00:15:58,360 --> 00:16:01,217
I've never seen anyone with
so much willpower before.

329
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:02,740
Now I know he can do it.

330
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:05,240
He can beat Moria! Whoa!

331
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:06,977
That's all of him!

332
00:16:07,060 --> 00:16:09,720
He took all 100 shadows! Unbelievable!

333
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:14,077
Uh, hey, buddy, you doing
okay with all those shadows?

334
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,807
Still feeling like yourself?

335
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:18,018
You're still Straw Hat Luffy, right?

336
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:19,600
Oh, yeah.

337
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:22,280
It's me.

338
00:16:25,540 --> 00:16:28,020
I'm getting stronger and stronger.

339
00:16:28,380 --> 00:16:29,820
I can feel it.

340
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:32,117
He seems kind of different, you know?

341
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:34,520
I mean, it's not my imagination, is it?

342
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:37,437
Because I'm pretty sure
he used to be smaller.

343
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:38,350
It's beautiful.

344
00:16:38,433 --> 00:16:41,379
I feel like I want to propose
to him all over again.

345
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,740
They all want to fight.

346
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:46,000
The shadows want to fight now!

347
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:48,720
Then let them go wild.

348
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:50,997
Hurry, there's not much time.

349
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:53,797
Just ten minutes to show
Moria the meaning of terror.

350
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:55,617
It's time to escape from this hell.

351
00:16:55,700 --> 00:16:57,524
Now get going, Nightmare Loopy!

352
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:04,800
I'm coming for you, Moria!

353
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:08,280
Hey, come back!

354
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:10,900
The mansion's the other way!

355
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,620
Here it comes!

356
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:26,080
This whole stretching
thing makes fighting fun!

357
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:28,180
Come back!

358
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:40,457
What the hell's going on here?

359
00:17:40,540 --> 00:17:42,893
He just got exponentially more powerful.

360
00:17:43,100 --> 00:17:46,577
It's not like he ate a Devil Fruit,
so how's he able to stretch like that?

361
00:17:46,660 --> 00:17:47,836
It's gotta be Mario.

362
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:48,842
What did he do?

363
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:54,000
There you have it.

364
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:57,827
Now you know the nightmarish
power of the Shadow Shadow Fruit.

365
00:17:58,840 --> 00:17:59,899
Shadow Revolution.

366
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:06,330
Revolution?

367
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:10,237
A shadow is a helpless prisoner
to the body that casts it,

368
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:12,144
mimicking it like a reflection.

369
00:18:12,380 --> 00:18:16,217
The body and shadow are physically
fused to the same shapes and movements.

370
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:18,040
It's a basic law of nature.

371
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:21,077
But I freed Oz's shadow
from the dominance of Oz's

372
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:24,460
body and taken control of
its form with my own shadow.

373
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:28,680
I can now change the shape
of Oz's shadow as I wish,

374
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:32,841
thereby forcing Oz's body to match
and follow its every contortion.

375
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:34,280
As I said,

376
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:38,337
it's long-natured that the body and
shadow must always hold the same shape.

377
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:42,117
But now the shadow is no longer
the subordinate, but the master.

378
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:45,460
The body is forced to obey
any shape the shadow takes.

379
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:48,300
This is the power of shadow revolution.

380
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:51,134
Moria is even stronger than we thought.

381
00:18:51,220 --> 00:18:54,377
Even if Oz doesn't have a double
fruit power, he can still stretch.

382
00:18:54,460 --> 00:18:57,197
If Moria controls his shadow,
he can rewrite the rules.

383
00:18:57,280 --> 00:19:00,517
It's a bit of cold comfort to know
that Orz isn't actually a rubber man.

384
00:19:00,600 --> 00:19:03,477
If he has all the same powers,
it doesn't do us much good.

385
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:05,197
Wasn't he tough enough already?

386
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:06,617
I mean, give us a break here.

387
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:07,530
Right?

388
00:19:07,613 --> 00:19:10,080
It was hard before, but
now it's almost impossible.

389
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:14,560
You know, he has even more
tricks than Straw Hat.

390
00:19:14,780 --> 00:19:18,500
For example, if I force
his shadow into a ball...

391
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:22,660
Orz will become a ball as well!

392
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:27,240
Oh, Spawn!

393
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:30,060
Dodge this. Roll!

394
00:19:33,220 --> 00:19:34,640
Um... Okay.

395
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:40,030
Huh?

396
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:44,200
Come on, Master.

397
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:46,320
What's the big idea here, huh?

398
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:47,800
This is my fight.

399
00:19:47,940 --> 00:19:50,020
I should get to try. Kashi!

400
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:51,680
I'm sorry.

401
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:53,508
I didn't mean to interfere.

402
00:19:53,740 --> 00:19:56,211
I'll just focus on assisting from here on.

403
00:19:56,520 --> 00:20:00,120
And now, crush each one of
them however you see fit.

404
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:06,680
Get back here, Zoro!

405
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:07,917
Don't be reckless!

406
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,941
Hey, this just occurred
to me, but where is Luffy?

407
00:20:11,180 --> 00:20:13,597
He ran off after Moria
and got tricked somehow.

408
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:15,637
I'm sure he's going to
be back soon, though!

409
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:16,550
Seriously?

410
00:20:16,633 --> 00:20:19,365
Does he have to do
something stupid every time?

411
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:20,737
What should I do?

412
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:21,650
Oh,

413
00:20:21,733 --> 00:20:23,417
it probably won't help if
I tell them another one

414
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:25,917
of the seven warlords is
somewhere on the island.

415
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,353
I'll get to that later.

416
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:31,117
Okay, I know I'm a little late to the
party, but let me get this straight.

417
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:33,197
Are you saying we've got
to defeat Luffy, Zombie,

418
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:36,017
and Moria if we want to get
everyone's shadows back?

419
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:37,720
Is that the gist of it?

420
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:40,280
Yeah, that's about it. You're kidding!

421
00:20:40,560 --> 00:20:41,977
The sun is almost up!

422
00:20:42,060 --> 00:20:43,697
The enemy is forcing our hand here.

423
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:45,297
It's not like we have much of a choice!

424
00:20:45,380 --> 00:20:46,420
Excuse me! Huh?

425
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:48,130
The skeleton?

426
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:50,341
I didn't know you were here, too.

427
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:51,717
I beg of you.

428
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:53,271
Please, allow me to help.

429
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:55,638
I have an idea that just might work.

430
00:20:57,900 --> 00:21:00,860
My friends, I appreciate your trust in me.

431
00:21:01,140 --> 00:21:03,497
I don't think it should be
too tough to pull it off.

432
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:05,117
Are you sure about this, Brooke?

433
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:07,117
I'm not trying to talk
you out of it or anything,

434
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,597
but you saw what happened to Franky,

435
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:09,510
right?

436
00:21:09,593 --> 00:21:11,257
Don't blame me if
anything goes wrong, okay?

437
00:21:11,340 --> 00:21:14,105
But if this is what you
want, I'm glad to help.

438
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:16,300
Now, Dark Cloud Tempo!

439
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:25,360
I'm ready fire at will i can't
believe we're using this thing again?

440
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:30,775
There's one thing i fear more than
death being unable to repay my debts.

441
00:21:33,260 --> 00:21:38,560
I'll fight to the last bone you can
count on me right try not to die!

442
00:21:49,740 --> 00:21:52,337
I'm getting such a shock
that I can see my bones!

443
00:21:52,420 --> 00:21:54,596
Well, I was only bones to begin with.

444
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:58,408
All right, here I come, like an
arrow, forced with lightning!

445
00:22:00,180 --> 00:22:01,240
Lightning bones!

446
00:22:02,380 --> 00:22:04,140
Come on, bone them all!

447
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:05,920
It worked!

448
00:22:06,140 --> 00:22:07,846
He shot straight through him!

449
00:22:08,560 --> 00:22:10,960
There's a hole in me! Now's our chance!

450
00:22:11,180 --> 00:22:12,180
Follow-up attack!

451
00:22:15,180 --> 00:22:17,877
As they say, mission accomplished.

452
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:19,820
Nice work there, Bones!

453
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:22,840
All right, two-sword style.

454
00:22:23,380 --> 00:22:24,280
Tower climb!

455
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:31,060
You bastard!

456
00:22:31,460 --> 00:22:32,400
You're next!

457
00:22:32,560 --> 00:22:36,600
But first, that skeleton's
gonna pay for hurting me!

458
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:37,980
Go, go!

459
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:39,330
Oh, no!

460
00:22:39,413 --> 00:22:41,660
He's going after Brock! Relax!

461
00:22:43,100 --> 00:22:45,160
Brock, no! Skeleton!

462
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:56,180
Take this!

463
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:57,960
Atlas Comet!

464
00:23:05,140 --> 00:23:06,540
Didn't work!

465
00:23:09,380 --> 00:23:10,440
Oh, crap.

466
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:11,875
Keep fighting, Usopp!

467
00:23:12,620 --> 00:23:14,100
Hey, what about you?

468
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:17,660
You just made yourself next, long-nosed.

469
00:23:17,960 --> 00:23:20,700
Your friend with the swords can wait!

470
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:30,020
I'm a dead man!

471
00:23:40,980 --> 00:23:43,980
Why can't I stretch?

472
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,420
Tochente fleur, Katorea manos.

473
00:23:54,620 --> 00:23:56,597
Where'd all these hands come from?

474
00:23:56,680 --> 00:23:57,680
That's cheating!

475
00:23:58,560 --> 00:24:00,860
Give it up, or I'll snap your neck!

476
00:24:01,100 --> 00:24:02,924
Your shadow revolution is over!
